                    {
                        "sense_id": "f45d694e-6dc1-3428-ba31-69cdc89e485d",
                        "entry_id": "ba25dbe2-53dc-3826-a4ed-e24a5dacdd0a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Exhibiting a love of or tendency toward sophistry; pertaining to spurious philosophy."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bd2a3e54-4072-4d15-8c0f-f2dd2ec9227a",
                                "sense_id": "f45d694e-6dc1-3428-ba31-69cdc89e485d",
                                "text": "That many philosophistic and superstitious conceits have been mixed with it, in process of time, proves nothing against the general fact as stated."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6bfbc7d8-6e56-43dd-845f-a29316b21fe1",
                                "sense_id": "f45d694e-6dc1-3428-ba31-69cdc89e485d",
                                "text": "A philosophy of the French Revolution should take care to avoid such philosphistic procedures."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f38a5455-cfcb-4741-92bf-8de0e68538df",
                                "sense_id": "f45d694e-6dc1-3428-ba31-69cdc89e485d",
                                "text": "This premodern pitilessness Pettigrew deprecated, but he was less enthusiastic about aspects of modernity other than compassion, like “atheism, deism, and philosophistic religion, so prevalent in the soi-disant enlightened countries."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "de92081f-e168-4f66-9dcd-ee20f347d83c",
                                "sense_id": "f45d694e-6dc1-3428-ba31-69cdc89e485d",
                                "text": "The real epochs are not exempt from philosophistic caprices; the ideal sometimes become converted into a mythology (though full of profound meanings)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
